# Marketing site

The public marketing site lives in `site/` (`@stream-kit/site`). Dark-only. English copy for now.

The site is **calm**: lots of whitespace, large Outfit headings, few lines. It shares the app's tokens, fonts, radius scale and `@stream-kit/ui` components, but **not** the blueprint chrome (no `GridFrame`, `SectionRule`, `Crosshair`, `CellGrid`, numbered `Eyebrow`s or `blueprint-*` backgrounds).

## Route groups

| Group / path | Chrome |
| --- | --- |
| `(marketing)/*` | Sticky header, footer — marketing chrome |
| `/app/*` | **No** marketing chrome (overlay host today; future logged-in dashboard) |

Keep marketing chrome in `(marketing)/+layout.svelte` only. Never wrap `/app` routes with the marketing header/footer.

## Layout

- Content column: `mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6` (narrower `max-w-3xl`/`max-w-4xl` for FAQ, pricing, hero copy).
- Sections are separated by whitespace (`py-24 sm:py-32`), not rules. At most an occasional `bg-sidebar` band with `border-y border-rule` (How it works, Pricing).
- Header: sticky, translucent `bg-background/80 backdrop-blur-md`, hairline only after scrolling; plain `text-sm` links, `Button size="sm"` download; hamburger menu below `md`.
- Footer belongs in the marketing layout (shared across `/`, `/plugins`, …), not duplicated per page.

## Structure

- Homepage = composition only. Each section is a component in `site/src/lib/components/marketing/` (`hero`, `integrations`, `how-it-works`, `features`, `plugins-overview`, `power-users`, `pricing`, `faq`, `final-cta`).
- Copy lives in `site/src/lib/marketing/content.ts`; URLs (`DOWNLOAD_URL`, `DOCS_URL`, `GITHUB_URL`, `docsUrl()`) in `site/src/lib/marketing/links.ts`. Never hardcode a download link.
- Section intros use `SectionHeading` (`components/marketing/section-heading.svelte`): small `text-primary` label → Outfit heading → muted lede. Page intros pass `as="h1"`.
- Product visuals are HTML mocks in `components/marketing/mocks/`, wrapped in `MockFrame` (decorative, `aria-hidden`). `app-mock.svelte` mirrors the real app shell (`packages/app/src/routes/+layout.svelte`, page header, nav item states) — update it when the shell changes.

## Page metadata

Every public page must set `<svelte:head>` with a unique `title` and `meta name="description"`.

## Visual language

- Same radius scale as the app: surfaces `rounded-xl`, controls `rounded-lg`, icon tiles/items `rounded-md`–`rounded-lg`.
- Lines `border-rule`; cards and lists `Panel tone="solid"` or `bg-surface` + `border-rule`.
- Controls: `@stream-kit/ui/button`, `@stream-kit/ui/input`, `Badge` — no hand-rolled fields or chips.
- No decorative gradients or glow blobs; depth comes from `bg-surface` and `shadow-2xl shadow-black/40` on mocks only.
- Mono only for code-like content (variables, file names, timestamps), not for labels or nav.

## Copy

- Tone: direct, product-focused, no hype filler or unverifiable claims ("lightweight", "under a minute", "join thousands").
- Every claim must match `docs/` and the plugin manifests: free app + optional **Pro** (cloud sync, cloud files, cloud overlays, AI Actions); Windows 10/11 only; early access; supported integrations only (no Kick/TikTok).
- Mention Streamer.bot only in the FAQ.
- English only until i18n is introduced.

## Stack reminders

- SvelteKit + Tailwind v4 + `@stream-kit/ui`
- PocketBase for plugin catalog (see `pocketbase.mdc`)
- Do not import Tauri APIs in `site/`
- `@stream-kit/ui/input` needs `bits-ui`, `runed` and `svelte-toolbelt` in `ssr.noExternal` (`site/vite.config.ts`)
